{"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/init(realm:asURI:pat:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/asURI","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/pat","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/realm"],"title":"Instance Properties"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13UmaChallengerV","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","title":"UmaChallenger","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UmaChallenger"}],"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UmaChallenger"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UmaChallenger"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Hand one to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamGuards\/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and a denial stops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"being a bare 403: the guard mints a fresh permission ticket for the pair the caller lacked and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches it to the thrown ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", so the framework adapter can return it as a header and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a UMA-aware client knows where to go for authority instead of only being told “no”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in, and deliberately so."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Emitting a challenge means minting a credential — a wire call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the Protection API, and a live ticket, produced on a path the caller did not explicitly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request. A guard that did that on every denial by default would turn each unauthorized request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into a Protection API call, which is a denial-of-service amplifier pointed at your own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"authorization server. So it happens only where an application asked for it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Failure is not escalation."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" If minting fails — the PAT expired, the Protection API is down,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the resource declares none of the requested scopes — the denial still surfaces as an ordinary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" without a challenge. A caller who was going to be refused is refused either way;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"letting a Protection API outage turn a deny into a 503 would hand the outage a second","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consequence, and letting it turn into an allow would be a security bug.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A configured "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WWW-Authenticate: UMA"},{"type":"text","text":" challenge emitter (CONTRACT.md §20.3, emit half)."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UmaChallenger","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A configured "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WWW-Authenticate: UMA"},{"type":"text","text":" challenge emitter (CONTRACT.md §20.3, emit half)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamClient/umaDiscover()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/umaDiscover()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"umaDiscover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Uma2Configuration","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK17Uma2ConfigurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"umaDiscover()","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/umadiscover()","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GET \/.well-known\/uma2-configuration"},{"type":"text","text":" (§20.1) — fetch the UMA discovery document."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/pat":{"title":"pat","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger\/pat","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/pat","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"pat","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sensitive","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK9SensitiveV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A Protection API Token: a ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"client-credentials"}]},{"text":" token carrying the ","type":"text"},{"code":"uma_protection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" scope","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(§20.2 rule 1). A user token cannot stand in — a minted ticket is bound to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that minted it.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/asURI":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/asURI","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger\/asuri","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The authorization server the caller should redeem the ticket at — normally this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deployment’s issuer, read from "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/umaDiscover()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" rather than concatenated by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hand, for the same reason §12.3 rule 6 gives."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"asURI","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"asURI"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/UmaChallenger/init(realm:asURI:pat:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/init(realm:asURI:pat:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"realm","kind":"